    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "War and hatte",
     "texto": [
      "For the past of «to be» and «to have», German almost always uses a simple form: **war** (was, were) and **hatte** (had).",
      "**Ich war zu Hause** (I was at home), **Ich hatte keinen Hunger** (I wasn't hungry).",
      "The **ich** and **er** forms are the same, with no ending."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
